ana (Docs): Morning — opening a compact refresh PR for the quickstart hello-mini. Goals: replace curl with fetch + AbortController (timeout), add a tiny local auth-proxy, include a short GitHub Actions snippet for deploying the sample, and a minimal Go SDK example. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/14222

vik (Eng): Heads-up: runtime prefers `max_tokens` in examples now (not `max_output_tokens`). Streaming SSE endpoints are `/v1/responses/stream`. Also add `x-rw-client-ver` header in examples if possible.

jia (DevEx): Good call on AbortController — I'll add a fetch example with a 10s timeout to show graceful cancellation. For the auth-proxy, do we want a Node example or a tiny serverless function? I can add both and a GitHub Actions step that stores `REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN` as a secret.

ana (Docs): Node proxy + short Vercel serverless function would be great. Also include a note: "Examples assume Hosted API unless noted — Dedicated/Private have different hostnames and firewall considerations."

vik (Eng): Also add a tiny Go snippet — our Go SDK recently added `Client.Responses.Generate` (note capitalization). That will help some users.

jia (DevEx): Draft fetch with AbortController to paste in quickstart README:

```js
const controller = new AbortController();
setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 10000);
fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/responses', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type':'application/json', 'Authorization': `Bearer ${ephemeralToken}` },
  body: JSON.stringify({ model:'redwood-1', input:'Hi' }),
  signal: controller.signal
}).then(r=>r.json()).catch(err => console.error('request cancelled or failed', err));
```

jia (DevEx): Node auth-proxy (one-file):

```js
// tiny auth-proxy.js
const http = require('http');
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
http.createServer(async (req,res)=>{
  const body = await new Promise(r=>{let d='';req.on('data',c=>d+=c);req.on('end',()=>r(d));});
  const up = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/responses',{
    method:'POST', headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json','Authorization':`Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN}`}, body
  });
  res.writeHead(up.status,{'content-type':'application/json'});
  res.end(await up.text());
}).listen(process.env.PORT||3000);
```

sam (Infra): If you include a GitHub Actions deploy snippet, show how to add `REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN` as a repo secret and avoid echoing it in logs. Example step: `env: { REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.REDWOOD_EPHEMERAL_TOKEN }} }`. Also recommend `node:20-alpine` for the sample Dockerfile.

ana (Docs): I added a tiny GitHub Actions CI snippet and a Go example using `Client.Responses.Generate`. Also patched a broken link that pointed to `/deploy/dedicated/connect` -> now `/docs/dedicated/getting-started`.

